### Street life: people the city throws at you.

=== enc_dealer
-- start
? hostile.darkarmy -> start_plain
DEALER: You look like a man who needs something he can't get at a pharmacy. Or a man who has something to sell. Either way, keep your hands where I can see them.
* "Let's see what you've got." -> trade
* "What do you buy?" -> buys
* [SPEECH 40] "Who's your supplier? I might have work for them." -> supplier | brush
* "Not interested." -> END
-- start_plain
DEALER: Quiet night. Keep it that way. You buying?
* "Show me." -> trade
* "No." -> END
-- trade
! barter fence
-> END
-- buys
DEALER: Cards, drives, jewelry, guns with the serials filed off. I pay less than a pawn shop and ask fewer questions than a priest.
* "Let's trade." -> trade
* "Maybe later." -> END
-- supplier
DEALER: ...Down by the piers there's a man who calls himself the Candyman. Everything on these corners comes through him. You didn't hear that from me. You didn't hear anything from me.
! set heard_candyman
-> END
-- brush
DEALER: Nice try. Buy something or keep walking.
-> END
